# Frontend UI standard

When adding or changing UI in `frontend/`:

## Component sources

1. **shadcn/ui** (`app/components/ui/`) — buttons, cards, badges, forms, dialogs, and all standard interactive UI. Install with `npx shadcn@latest add <component>`.
2. **Aceternity UI** (`app/components/aceternity/`) — motion, backgrounds, spotlight, 3D effects, and other stylized visuals. Install with `npx shadcn@latest add @aceternity/<name>`. Move files from `frontend/components/` into `app/components/aceternity/` if the CLI uses the wrong path.
3. **Tailwind / CSS** — **layout only** on routes and wrappers: flex, grid, gap, width, max-width, padding, positioning, breakpoints.

## Do

- Compose pages from shadcn + Aceternity components
- Use shadcn variants and theme tokens (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `variant="outline"`)
- Use Aceternity for effects; keep shadcn for the underlying UI primitives
- Put palette changes in `app/app.css` (`:root` / `.dark`)
- Use `@phosphor-icons/react` for icons

## Do not

- Build custom styled buttons, cards, or badges from scratch when shadcn has them
- Use Tailwind color, border, shadow, or typography utilities to style leaf UI instead of shadcn/Aceternity
- Add heavy animation libraries for effects Aceternity already provides
- Commit Aceternity files under `frontend/components/` — they belong in `app/components/aceternity/`

